vLLM 0.34 builds a model's vision tower on the meta device on every pipeline rank after the first
(_mark_tower_model now applies no_init_weights there unconditionally; 0.33 did so only under the v2 model
runner) and replaces it with a stage stub. vision-tower-cpu-offload wraps the tower's merger and blocks in a
UVA offloader inside the tower's constructor, and the offloader's copy to host raised "Cannot copy out of meta
tensor" on rank 1, so VISION=1 with VLLM_VISION_CPU_OFFLOAD_GB at PP=2 could not boot (2x RTX 3090, the #328
PP=2 profile). The offloader is now skipped when the tower is being built on the meta device. A tower built
for real is offloaded as before.

Kind: own
What: skip the vision tower's CPU offload on pipeline ranks that build the tower on the meta device, so
  VISION=1 with VLLM_VISION_CPU_OFFLOAD_GB boots at PP=2 on 0.34
Upstream: none
Cut-against: 0.34.0
Retires-when: rides with vision-tower-cpu-offload

